  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason includes computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (2333.33) and evaluating which lottery has a higher probability of exceeding this level. The individual, however, does not consider such a mean or any neutral reference point derived from all outcomes. Instead, the individual uses 3000 Euros (the outcome of A) as a reference point and interprets deviations from it in loss terms. This reflects a loss-aversion or certainty-bias reasoning, not an aspiration-level rule based on the mean of all outcomes. The justification is grounded in perceived loss relative to the sure gain, not in the probability of exceeding a computed aspiration level. While both the reason and the individual prefer Lottery A, the underlying logic differs. There is no evidence that the individual calculated or considered the mean of all outcomes or evaluated outcomes relative to such a mean. The reasoning process described is inconsistent with the aspiration-level rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
